@flexiarg cascade-construction/choose-the-grain-where-state-lives
@title Choose The Cascade's Grain Where Its State Naturally Lives
@keywords grain, universe, per-item, per-cycle, per-repo, quantifier, adapter
@audience agents constructing cascades, interpretation admission
@tone technical
@style pattern
@status draft 2026-09-17 (claude-7; finding F5, worked instances 2026-09-16)
@references [pattern-interpretation/declare-the-universe cascade-construction/order-by-what-each-step-needs hygiene/exempt-the-in-use]
@see-also cascades/the-slice-is-the-unit-of-use
@why the grain decides how many facts the cascade reasons over and whether its guards can be written at all. Too fine and the universe explodes and needs quantifiers the guard language lacks; too coarse and the facts stop meaning anything observable.
@how choose the unit whose state one run of the cascade changes and whose facts can each be observed: a cleaning cycle, a repository, a handoff × namespace pair. Keep invariants over many items inside that unit (every modified buffer is protected) in the adapter and the gate, and expose only their outcome as a fact (exemptions-recorded). Record the chosen grain with the universe.
@violation-signature a buffer-cleaner cascade grounded per buffer (134 buffers × about 5 facts ≈ 670 facts); a fleet-wide inbox-zero fact that is true when any one repo is clean; a test-registry fact about "the review" when lanes differ per namespace.
! conclusion: Pick the grain whose state one run changes and whose facts are observable, and keep many-item invariants in adapters and gates.

  + context: The same problem can be modelled per item, per batch or per system.

  + IF:
    A cascade's fact universe is being declared.

  + HOWEVER:
    Requirements are often stated per item ("never kill a modified buffer").

  + THEN:
    Model at the unit one run changes and push per-item rules into the gate.

  + BECAUSE:
    The cascade has to be scored and enacted; the gate has to enforce the per-item rule anyway.

  + evidence: buffer cleaner at cycle grain (9 facts); inbox zero at repo grain (16 facts for p4ng); test registry at handoff × namespace grain, where cascade_model_manifest_test and receipt_construction_test took full reruns and shadow_cascade_g_test a spot-check on futon2 cb5f8b1288.
